<PolicyPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Learn what information Alohomora Chocolate Circle collects for Chocolate Circle orders and how it is used."
  kicker="Your information, handled thoughtfully"
>
  <p>
    <strong>Effective date: 22 October 2026.</strong> This notice describes the information used
    to operate Chocolate Circle, take orders, arrange delivery, and provide customer accounts.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible for your information</h2>
  <p>
    The shop is operated by <strong>Alohomora Chocolate Circle</strong>, trading as Chocolate
    Circle. The business address and dispatch location are M3, Pushpammal St, RG Nagar,
    Krishnaveni Nagar, Medavakkam, Vengavasal, Tamil Nadu 600073. The food business FSSAI
    registration number provided by the operator is <strong>22420076002595</strong>. The shop is
    not registered for GST. For privacy questions or requests, contact
    <a href="mailto:alohomora.chocolatecircle@gmail.com">alohomora.chocolatecircle@gmail.com</a>
    or WhatsApp <a href="https://wa.me/919500868468">+91 95008 68468</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
  <p>
    When you sign in, we use your email address to send a one-time sign-in code and associate
    your customer profile and orders. A new customer can save a name, mobile number, street
    address, city, state, and PIN code. You may edit those details for an individual order; the
    event date is collected for that order only. We also keep order items, prices, payment and
    order references, payment/order status, delivery method, and the delivery address used for
    each order. Manual orders entered by the shop are associated with your profile when they use
    your email address.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you enter a PIN code, the shop’s Worker looks it up with public PIN-code and map-data
    services (India Post PIN directory data and OpenStreetMap Nominatim) to fill in your city and
    state and to find the PIN code’s approximate location. Only the PIN code is sent to those
    services. The approximate location is used to calculate straight-line distance from the shop
    and suggest Porter at or within 15 km, or a courier beyond 15 km. Coordinates are not saved in
    the shop’s order database or included in Razorpay order notes.
  </p>

  <h2>3. How we use and share information</h2>
  <p>
    We use customer and order information to create and manage your profile, process product
    payments, contact you about your order, confirm the delivery fee and arrangements, deliver
    your purchase, maintain business records, and respond to questions or complaints. The shop
    may contact you using the email address or phone number you provide, including by WhatsApp
    where appropriate.
  </p>
  <p>
    Razorpay processes product payments and receives order information needed to create and
    verify a payment.     India Post PIN directory data and OpenStreetMap Nominatim provide
        PIN-code lookup. Resend delivers sign-in codes. Cloudflare runs the order Worker and stores
    customer and order records in D1. GitHub Pages hosts the static website. Delivery providers
    receive the contact and address details needed to fulfil a delivery after arrangements are
    confirmed. WhatsApp may process messages when you contact or are contacted through WhatsApp.
    These providers process information under their own terms and privacy notices. The site does
    not collect or store full card or bank credentials and does not currently use advertising
    analytics or subscribe customers to marketing messages.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Storage and retention</h2>
  <p>
    Customer profiles and order records are stored in the shop’s Cloudflare D1 database. Sign-in
    codes and server-side session tokens are stored as hashes; codes expire after 10 minutes and
    sign-in sessions after 30 days. Your browser stores the session token for the current tab by
    default. If you select “Remember me on this device,” it is kept in that browser’s local
    storage until you sign out or the server session expires. The shopping bag is also stored in
    your browser’s local storage. The shop
    currently has no fixed automatic deletion schedule for customer and order records; records
    are retained for shop operations and applicable Indian legal and recordkeeping requirements.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Your requests</h2>
  <p>
    You may contact us to request access to or correction of your profile, or to ask for deletion
    of information. We will consider and respond to requests under applicable law. We may need
    to retain some order, payment, or accounting records where required by law or needed to
    resolve a transaction or dispute. Send requests to
    <a href="mailto:alohomora.chocolatecircle@gmail.com">alohomora.chocolatecircle@gmail.com</a>
    or WhatsApp <a href="https://wa.me/919500868468">+91 95008 68468</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Security and children</h2>
  <p>
    Payment credentials are handled by Razorpay rather than stored by this website. The shop
    uses account access controls for its order database, but no internet transmission or storage
    method can be guaranteed completely secure. If you have a concern about information
    associated with your account or a suspected privacy incident, contact us promptly using the
    details above.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Updates</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this notice when our services or practices change. The current version and its
    effective date will be posted on this page.
  </p>
</PolicyPage>
